From 109702d789c8a6589ad05bf22258335a03ab8e57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jared Massie <you@example.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:21:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add in-person PIN unlock with mandatory tamper alert
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a numeric PIN (set up in Settings, salted SHA-256 hash only —
the PIN itself is never stored) that unlocks a blocked app or site
immediately on-device, for when the approval partner is physically
present instead of reachable by email. Bypassing the usual approval
step is the whole point, so using the PIN always fires the same
tamper-alert email/text used for uninstall attempts and
accessibility/VPN tampering, so it can never be used quietly.
